# Copy this file to .env before running `docker compose up --build`.
# Nothing here costs money or needs an account - the whole stack runs on free,
# self-hosted/public services:
#   - Map: Leaflet.js + OpenStreetMap tiles (no key)
#   - Directions: the public OSRM demo routing API (no key)
#   - AI assistant: Ollama running locally in its own container (no key)
#
# This file only exists so OLLAMA_MODEL is overridable without editing
# docker-compose.yml directly.

# Which Ollama model the assistant-service asks for. Defaults to llama3.2:1b
# (~1.3GB) if unset - picked to be realistic on a slow/limited connection.
# The ollama container pulls this model automatically on first `docker compose
# up` (one-time only, cached after that - see README). If you have more
# bandwidth to spare, a bigger model (e.g. llama3, ~4.7GB) will generally
# answer better - just set OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3 here.
OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2:1b
